    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. $\\frac{35}{80}\\ne\\frac{45}{80}\\times\\frac{55}{80}$.",
      "worked": "Let $A$ be the event that an adult is less than 30 years old and $G$ the event that they play computer games more than once a week.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap G)&=\\frac{35}{80}=\\frac{7}{16}\\\\P(A)\\times P(G)&=\\frac{45}{80}\\times\\frac{55}{80}\\\\P(A)\\times P(G)&=\\frac{99}{256}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac{7}{16}=\\frac{112}{256}\\ne\\frac{99}{256}$, $P(A\\cap G)\\ne P(A)\\times P(G)$. Therefore, playing computer games multiple times a week is not independent of age category.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
